from the direction of travel","source":"geometric convention separating walking along a roadway from crossing it, from pedestrian heading resolution"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"traffic-conflict technique (Swedish TCT, Hydén 1987): time-to-collision thresholds of 1.5 to 3 s"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"AASHTO passenger-car design vehicle dimensions (about 5.8 m by 2.1 m)"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
